# Auth

Two layers; do not collapse them.

1. `proxy.ts` — optimistic cookie check on `/dashboard/:path*` only. No cookie → `/login?next=…`. Does not validate the session.
2. `requireSession()` in `lib/session.ts` — real Better Auth session. Use in dashboard layouts/pages and server actions. No session → `/login`.
3. `requireGuest()` — signed-in users hitting `/login` or `/signup` → `safeNext(?next)` (internal path only, else `/dashboard`).

- Guest-only pages: `/login`, `/signup`. Keep `/` public even when logged in.
- `?next=` must go through `safeNext` (starts with `/`, not `//`).
- Client auth: `lib/auth-client.ts` + `components/auth/auth-form.tsx`. Route handler: `app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts`.
- Reads (`listFavorites`, `getProfile`) live in `lib/db/queries.ts`, not `"use server"` files. Actions take the user id from `requireSession()` only.
